From 1fa91dd2953bbeadf3d74a47ea621c71c1686cdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: agenticarus <icarus@seb-server.xyz>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:03:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: tolerate JSONC in mcp.json so one comment doesn't drop
 every MCP server

The Kiro IDE accepts JSONC in ~/.kiro/settings/mcp.json, but the reader used strict json.loads, so one // comment made every MCP server in the file vanish. Adds a string-aware strip_jsonc helper plus tolerant retry in _load_mcp_json_by_source (broken files still log-and-skip; tolerated parses keep written configs JSON-clean by refusing rather than silently stripping), and api_mcp_sync now retries through the same helper and refuses a destructive rewrite (500) instead of resetting the file. The disconnect path propagates the refusal via a preflight check in ownership.py. 12 new tests in test_mcp_discovery_jsonc.py; sync/refusal coverage extended.
---
